[ECO "C52"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pawn-grab"]
[Themes "centre-fight,lead-in-development"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "4...Bxb4 5.c3 Ba5"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3"]

5... Ba5 6. d4 { Takes the centre and attacks e5. White now has two pawns in the middle and Black's king is still uncastled. } 6... exd4 7. O-O { Castles first. The bishop on a5 [pins the c3 pawn](r1bqk1nr/pppp1ppp/2n5/b7/2BpP3/2P2N2/P4PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq -) to the king, so cxd4 is not legal yet; castling ends the pin and gets the king safe. } 7... d6 ( 7... Nge7 8. cxd4 { Now the pawn can retake, because the king has left the diagonal. } 8... d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Ba3 { Stops Black castling: the bishop covers f8. Black's king is stuck in the middle while White's pieces come out. } 10... Be6 ) ( 7... Nf6 8. cxd4 { Retakes the pawn, so White has a strong centre for free. } 8... d6 9. d5 { Drives the knight from c6 before Black can arrange pieces around it. } 9... Ne7 10. e5 { Opens the position while White has the better development. } ) 8. cxd4 { Retakes and wins the pawn back. White has two big pawns in the centre and Black must watch for d5 and e5. } 8... Bb6 9. Nc3 { Another piece into play, and it defends the e4 pawn. White has fewer pawns but more active pieces. } 9... Na5 ( 9... Bg4 10. Bb5 { Pins the knight on c6 to the king and adds to the pressure on d4. } 10... Bxf3 11. gxf3 { Retakes towards the centre and opens the g-file for the rook. White keeps the bishop pair. } 11... a6 12. Ba4 ) ( 9... Nf6 10. e5 { Hits the knight before Black is ready. Black's king is still in the middle, so opening the centre favours White. } 10... dxe5 11. Ba3 ) 10. Bd3 { Steps out of reach of the knight, which wanted to take the bishop for free. The bishop keeps pointing at h7. } 10... Nge7 11. h3 { Stops ...Bg4, which would pin the knight on f3. Plan: Re1, then Bg5 or Ne2 and Bf4; look for d5 and e5 breaks. If Black leaves the book, castle, hold the centre and keep developing. } *
